      "message": "Not a blocker for this change, but could we follow up on this separately? `cnat_output_feature_new_flow_inline()` treats a SNAT address as available when `ce_ip` is nonzero, whereas the direct SNAT path uses `CNAT_EP_FLAG_RESOLVED`. After an interface loses its last address, the resolver clears that flag but retains the cached address, so this path can keep selecting the stale address. Checking `RESOLVED` here would make both paths consistent.",
